 "traps": [
  "Blazor has no package of its own: OpenBudgeteer.Blazor uses the Web SDK and AddRazorComponents().AddInteractiveServerComponents() in Program.cs; MudBlazor is its component framework",
  "Entity Framework Core is spread over eight projects, among them three migrations projects for MySQL, PostgreSQL and a SQLite one",
  "SQLite is no longer a provider: the switch in DatabaseInitializationExtensions.cs accepts MARIADB, MYSQL, POSTGRES and POSTGRESQL, and OpenBudgeteer.Core.Data.Sqlite.Migrations is a leftover that targets net8.0 while every other project targets net10.0",
  "the databases appear only in the three examples/compose-*.yaml files and in CONNECTION_PROVIDER; phpMyAdmin and Adminer in those files are admin tools, not services of the application",
  "Redis is required at startup (AddRedis in Program.cs, CONNECTION_REDIS_* in examples/example.env), through StackExchange.Redis",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
